  "title": "Runabout: A mobile EEG study of auditory oddball processing in laboratory and real-world conditions",
  "description": "Raw and pre-processed mobile EEG recordings from 44 healthy adults performing an auditory oddball task with complex tone stimuli. The task was performed in three environments of increasing complexity: a quiet laboratory, a sports field, and a university campus route. In each environment participants either counted deviant tones or ignored the tones. The dataset supports investigation of how cognitive task demands, motor demands and environmental complexity affect attentional processing, and includes the MATLAB and R analysis pipeline.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded from 32 active electrodes using a Brain Vision LiveAmp 32 amplifier while participants completed an oddball task (piano and horn tones) in LAB, FIELD and CAMPUS settings, each under COUNT and IGNORE instructions. Preprocessing used EEGLAB, ERPLAB, ICLabel and clean_rawdata in MATLAB. Statistical analysis used mixed-effects models in R.",
